('128.36.c.6.C',2,'Which pronoun replaces ''Ana'' in ''Ana has a dog''?','["He", "She", "It", "They"]'::jsonb,1,'Ana is a girl, so she is the pronoun.','original'),
('128.36.c.6.D',2,'Making a list of ideas before writing is called:','["printing", "publishing", "prewriting", "proofreading"]'::jsonb,2,'Prewriting gathers ideas.','original'),
('128.36.c.6.D',2,'Which activity helps a writer plan?','["turning in the final copy", "erasing the page", "closing the notebook", "drawing a web of ideas"]'::jsonb,3,'Webs organize thoughts.','original'),
('128.36.c.6.E',2,'Which sentence is written in first person?','["I walked to the park with my friend.", "She walked to the park.", "The dog walked to the park.", "They walked to the park."]'::jsonb,0,'First person uses I.','original'),
('128.36.c.6.E',2,'First-person writing uses the pronoun:','["she", "I", "he", "they"]'::jsonb,1,'I is the first-person pronoun.','original'),
('128.36.c.6.F',2,'A learner raises a hand, then speaks in a complete sentence. This shows:','["avoiding speech", "breaking rules", "using classroom conventions", "writing a poem"]'::jsonb,2,'Conventions guide classroom talk.','original'),
