('128.36.c.6.I',3,'A chart of daily temperatures can be shown as:','["a line graph", "a recipe", "a letter", "a rhyme"]'::jsonb,0,'Line graphs show change over time.','original'),
('128.36.c.6.J',3,'Which greeting is more formal?','["Yo!", "Good afternoon, sir.", "Sup?", "Hey, what''s up?"]'::jsonb,1,'Formal language suits respectful settings.','original'),
('128.36.c.6.J',3,'Talking with a friend at recess usually uses:','["scientific language", "legal language", "informal language", "ceremonial language"]'::jsonb,2,'Informal language suits friends.','original'),
('128.36.c.6.K',2,'A word processor helps a writer to:','["bake a cake", "cut paper", "measure a desk", "type, revise and save writing"]'::jsonb,3,'Word processors are writing tools.','original'),
('128.36.c.6.K',2,'Spell-check in a writing program:','["flags possible spelling errors", "prints automatically", "writes the essay", "chooses the topic"]'::jsonb,0,'It helps editing.','original'),
('128.36.c.6.L',2,'Labeling a picture of a plant helps a learner to:','["skip the lesson", "remember the parts", "hide the picture", "forget the words"]'::jsonb,1,'Labels reinforce vocabulary.','original'),
('128.36.c.6.L',2,'Sketching a diagram while studying is a:','["school bell", "punishment", "study tool", "spelling test"]'::jsonb,2,'Sketches help memory.','original'),
('128.36.c.6.M',3,'A writer checks mechanics by looking at:','["pencil color", "paper brand", "desk size", "spelling, capitals and punctuation"]'::jsonb,3,'Mechanics are the conventions of writing.','original'),
('128.36.c.6.M',3,'Checking content means asking whether the writing:','["has clear and complete ideas", "has neat margins only", "has long words only", "has a nice cover"]'::jsonb,0,'Content concerns ideas.','original'),
('128.36.c.6.N',3,'Which word helps connect two ideas to show addition?','["under", "also", "blue", "never"]'::jsonb,1,'Also adds information.','original'),
('128.36.c.6.N',3,'First, next and finally help writing by showing:','["color", "size", "order", "weight"]'::jsonb,2,'They are sequence words.','original'),
('128.36.c.7.A',2,'To find facts about the moon, a learner can use:','["a menu", "a comic book only", "a game console", "an encyclopedia or reliable website"]'::jsonb,3,'Reference sources give facts.','original'),
('128.36.c.7.A',2,'A table of contents helps a learner:','["find a chapter in a book", "count the words", "sharpen a pencil", "measure a page"]'::jsonb,0,'It lists parts of a book.','original'),
('128.36.c.7.B',2,'Saving facts from several websites in one document is:','["hiding information", "compiling information with technology", "erasing information", "guessing information"]'::jsonb,1,'Technology helps gather information.','original'),
('128.36.c.7.B',2,'A learner can collect notes in a:','["lunch box", "pencil case", "digital notebook", "gym bag"]'::jsonb,2,'Digital notes are stored with technology.','original'),
